"Damp Tunnel"
"Damp limestone lines this cavern passage, condensation collecting on the cool
stone in such quantities that it sends droplets from the ceiling to form small
puddles on the cavern floor.  The cacophonous sound of rushing water assaults
the cavern from the west, amplified by echoes until it reaches a near-painful
intensity.  To the east, the terrain dips sharply, as the limestone cavern
drops into darkness.
"
